# Architecture governance for Rust: a crate depends on dca-rules, the DCA rule suite, whose `dca_tests!()` names
# each test after its rule id (`dca_tac_003`). The check runs those tests, then the two Clippy lints the crates'
# `clippy.toml` fill (disallowed types and methods), as errors. cargo-deny's bans stay the project's own line.
kind: governance
order: 20
detect.contains: **/Cargo.toml :: dca-rules
architecture: cargo test --workspace dca_ && cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D clippy::disallowed_types -D clippy::disallowed_methods
